[h1]R.A.T.S. Clean Screen[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]

[b]Your windows, no version label on top.[/b]
The Steam beta branch draws the game's own version label ("Sea Power v0.8.7-261107") above everything: on the title bars of windows, on the map and on the windows of other mods, popped-out ones included. This mod switches it off.

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*]The game's version label is gone
[*]Two ini lines and no code: a config patch that sets [b]ShowVersionWatermark=False[/b] in the game's own config. No mod loader needed
[*]Switch the mod off in the Mods menu and the label is back
[*]It changes nothing else in the game
[/list]

[h2]Install[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, and switch R.A.T.S. Clean Screen on in the game's Mods menu
[*]Restart the game
[/olist]
Run in the game on the 3D globe public beta (build 261107): a mission shows no version label with the mod on. 0.8.7 not run.

Source: [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerCleanScreen]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerCleanScreen[/url] (MIT)

[i]R.A.T.S. – Ratte's Assorted Tactical Systems[/i]
